:: MO-EA-EAPov {"position":"900,1250","size":"100,100"}
You:
“Mom, do you pay attention to the news?”
-
Mom:
“Of course. Why are you asking?”
-
You:
“It’s for a class. I have to write a report on a news story from my community.”
-
Mom:
“Oh, thats easy. The protest they did to stop the construction of a Tesla factory in East Austin. The city actually listened this time.”
-
You:
“Do they usually not work?”
-
Mom:
“Not for communities like ours, but sometimes we get a win.”
-
You:
“I didn’t know you were so into politics.”
-
Mom:
“Of course I am. We have to fight for ourselves.”
-
You:
(I haven’t given it much thought before. Maybe I should be more interested in my community.)
-
Do you want to become more active in your community?
