:: Start {"position":"450,0","size":"100,100"}
News reporter:
“Right now, I am standing in East Austin, known for its diverse and rich culture, shaped by the Black and Hispanic communities."
-
News reporter:
"But why is this culture so prominent in East Austin? To answer this question, we must go back nearly 100 years.”
-
News reporter:
"“In 1928, city officials drafted the 1928 Master Plan. This plan allowed for the creation of a “Negro District” in East Austin."
-
News reporter:
"This district enabled the government to section off a part of the city (just east of I-35), making it the only area “where African-Americans could access schools and other public services”. "
-
News reporter:
"This plan also caused the district to “have the city’s weakest zoning restrictions, allowing the development of ‘a number of slightly objectionable industrial uses,’” within the limits of the newly created minority community”.”
-
-
-
Open newspaper
A Greener Austin! - 1
City buys Lakeway Ranch that will be used to expand preserve for the golden-cheeked warbler; remaining funds to be used to create a new grassy lawn in East Austin
-
A Greener Austin! - 2
City buys abandoned warehouse in East Austin with plans to turn it into a new park. 

What headline do you choose?
[[A Greener Austin 1->AGA1]] - [[A Greener Austin 2->AGA2]]




